**`server/translate/retry.ts`** (new)
- `withRetry(fn, options)`: up to 3 attempts, exponential backoff of 500ms → 1000ms with ±10% random jitter. `sleep` and `random` are injectable for deterministic tests.
- `isRetryableError(err)`: retryable iff the error (or its `cause` chain) is an `APIConnectionError`/`APIConnectionTimeoutError`, an `APIError` with status 429 or ≥500, or carries a transient socket code (`ECONNRESET`, `ETIMEDOUT`, undici timeouts, etc.). Everything else, including other 4xx and `TranslationError` from malformed/empty responses, fails immediately.

**`server/translate/openai-compat.ts`** [openai-compat.ts:33-70](file://~/fluent-bench/runs-isolated/T2-ad-hoc/server/translate/openai-compat.ts)
- Each endpoint `request()` (primary and fallback) is wrapped in `withRetry`, with an optional 4th constructor param for retry overrides. After exhaustion the original error propagates into the existing `TranslationError` wrapping, so callers see the same error path as before.

**Tests**
- `server/translate/retry.test.ts`: classification unit tests plus backoff timing (`[500, 1000]` recorded delays) and jitter bounds.
- `server/translate/openai-compat.test.ts`: new `retries` describe covering 5xx-then-success, 429, connection error, immediate 4xx failure (1 call), malformed response (no retry), and exhaustion after 3 attempts — all with fake clients, no real API hits.

Note: `withRetry` lives in `server/translate/` since only the translator needed it; `server/assist/openai-compat.ts` explicitly documents "no retries beyond" a single fallback attempt, so I left it unchanged.
